  "checks": "One sanity pass over every reconstructed blockface subject: is it oriented, consistent and sane?\n\n`audit_structure.py` says whether the FILES are there. This says whether their CONTENTS are what we think,\nand it checks the things that have actually gone wrong in this project rather than a generic wish list:\n\n  ORIENT   the store's slice axis must run anterior -> posterior (negative step, slice 0 frontal). That is\n           the convention since 2026-09-19; see code/ORIENTATION.md.\n  MIRROR   the iso grey must agree with its own brain mask in WORLD space. A stray\n           `fix_ap_orientation.py apply` after a rebuild mirrors an already-correct grey against its mask,\n           which is invisible in any single volume and destroys every registration that uses the grey\n           (MF191 and MF204, 2026-09-20: dice 0.61 instead of 0.97, R3 NCC -0.013).\n  CHIRAL   the drill holes are in the LEFT hemisphere, so their centroid must sit at NEGATIVE world x\n           relative to the brain's. Left-right cannot be settled by fit quality on a near-symmetric brain\n           (MR261's two x-flips scored Dice 0.904 vs 0.902), so this marker is the only cheap check.\n  SIZE     L-R and D-V extent against the cohort. A subject 20 % off is a voxel-size error, not a brain.\n           (A-P is NOT checked: the cohort is truncated by varying amounts, which is real.)\n  ALIGN    frame-to-frame brain-centroid step through the stack - the alignment quality that the camera-jump\n           correction exists to deliver.\n",
